tengri independently implements models and algorithms described or used in
the following projects, and validates its implementations against them. In
each case the docstring of the relevant tengri function names the
corresponding upstream symbol and the published reference:

  Prospector (Johnson et al. 2021)
    https://github.com/bd-j/prospector
    add_igm (fake_fsps), psb_logsfr_ratios_to_agebins,
    zred_to_agebins_pbeta, line-placement routines, NLR helpers.

  FastSpecFit (Moustakas et al.)
    https://github.com/desihub/fastspecfit
    populate_emtable, LineMasker.

  AGNfitter / AGNfitter-rX (Calistro Rivera et al. 2016; Martínez-Ramírez et al.)
    https://github.com/GabrielaCR/AGNfitter
    BBB-related helpers; the Silva+2004 IR and SKIRTOR template data it
    publishes are repackaged as tengri input grids.

  CIGALE (Boquien et al. 2019)
    https://gitlab.lam.fr/cigale/cigale
    skirtor2016 (k_ext, agn_lnu_ir, adaf_disk), sfh_buat08, sfhdelayedbq,
    sfhperiodic, IRX module.

  ProSpect (Robotham et al.)
    https://github.com/asgr/ProSpect
    massfunc_p4 / massfunc_p6, massfunc_snorm_burst,
    massfunc_snorm_burst_trunc.

  RELAGN (Hagen & Done)
    https://github.com/scotthgn/RELAGN
    Used as a build-time dependency to precompute nthcomp template grids;
    tengri does not ship its solver.

Data products (filter curves, SSP grids, nebular grids) shipped under their
respective upstream licenses; see data/README.md for details.

Please cite upstream authors when publishing results that use tengri.
